<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Arghun dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1520 CE – 1554 CE (approx.) · capital Bhakkar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Turko-Mongol dynasty from Kandahar that conquered Sindh from the Sammas in the early 16th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arghun">Arghuns</a>, Turko-Mongol nobles who had served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid</a> rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a>, held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> drove them out in the 1510s. Their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-beg-arghun">Shah Beg Arghun</a> turned south, defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/samma-dynasty">Samma dynasty</a> in 1520 and established his rule in upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, with the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukkur">Bhakkar</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> as a key base.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-beg-arghun">Shah Beg</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-husain-arghun">Shah Husain Arghun</a> extended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arghun">Arghun</a> power to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thatta">Thatta</a> in lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> and north to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multan">Multan</a>, which he took from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/langah-sultanate">Langah Sultanate</a>. He opposed the fugitive Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humayun">Humayun</a>, who wandered in Sindh from 1541 to 1543 and failed to take Arghun strongholds. Arghun rule depended on Central Asian soldiers and was harsh on the local Samma and Soomra nobility.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1554, as the ailing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-husain-arghun">Shah Husain</a> lost control, his officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirza-isa-tarkhan">Mirza Isa Tarkhan</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thatta">Thatta</a> and founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tarkhan-dynasty">Tarkhan dynasty</a> in lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>. Shah Husain died childless in 1556, and upper Sindh later fell to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1520 CE – 1554 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.95%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1520 CE – 1554 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bhakkar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shah Beg Arghun, Shah Husain Arghun</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian, Chagatai</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, <a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arghuns of Sindh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1537&amp;focus=arghun-dynasty" aria-label="Arghun dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6512 1026 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Arghun dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6832 1282L6803 1523M6832 1282L6855 1331M6832 1282L6803 1523"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6803 1523h0M6855 1331h0M6803 1523h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6832 1282h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6832 1282h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bhakkar. <a href="/atlas?year=1537&amp;focus=arghun-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
